0..75 Comment "//! `niche-realizability` models a null niche as a realizability predicate."
76..79 Comment "//!"
80..266 Comment "//! A realiser is a predicate on a word and heap. `star` splits disjoint heaps. `pointsTo` describes a singleton. The normaliser computes assertions. The kernel replays each declaration."
267..270 Comment "//!"
271..483 Comment "//! `Option<&T>` uses one word for null or a reference. Its realisers equal the tagged layout at every heap. Marshallers meet their triples. `deref_or` meets the niche. The pathological source refuses `_Nonnull`."
484..487 Comment "//!"
488..504 Comment "//! - see: #2832"
505..536 Comment "//! - see: #327 — `derefOrWp`"
537..644 Comment "//! - see: `../../pathological/specification/niche-realizability.gandr` — the refused `_Nonnull` neighbor"
645..725 Comment "//! - cites: [Wagner-2024-realistic_realizability_specifying_abis_you_can_count]"
726..917 Comment "//! [Wagner-2024-realistic_realizability_specifying_abis_you_can_count]: https://doi.org/10.1145/3689755 \"Wagner, Eisbach and Ahmed, Realistic Realizability: Specifying ABIs You Can Count On\""
